   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to authorizing regional\nplanning council's eligibility to apply for federal and/or state grants",
    "basePrintNo": "S8958",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8958-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 43,
       "fullName": "Jake Ashby",
       "imgName": "971_Jake_Ashby.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1522,
       "sessionMemberId": 1885,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "ASHBY"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §239-h, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8958\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to authorizing\nregional planning council's eligibility to apply for federal and/or\nstate grants\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow for Regional Planning Councils the eligibility of state and\nfederal grants.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the general municipal law to allow Regional Planning Councils the\neligibility of state and federal grants.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRegional Planning Commissions as a rule work with local governments in a\ncoordinated and cooperative effort. They often coordinate local govern-\nment projects yet are not able to directly secure funding which can be a\nbarrier to or delay project completion.. Allowing RPCs to apply for\ngrants and funding will streamline the process which can help expedite\nimplementation of projects.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 180 days after enacted into law.\n",
